% ============================================================================
%  pricebook — bibliography
% ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
%  A BibTeX mirror of docs/references.md, for the Substack prose (FP-1) and any
%  LaTeX write-up. The citation keys match references.md EXACTLY, so a \cite in
%  a draft and a `source:` in a src/ header name the same thing.
%
%  references.md remains THE AUTHORITY: it carries each source's status
%  (in-hand / worked-from / named-but-not-in-hand), its per-tranche oracle use,
%  and — the material the series lives on — the source DEFECTS found. This file
%  carries none of that; it is the formal citation only. When the two disagree,
%  references.md wins and this file is regenerated.
%
%  The `keywords` field records our working status:
%    held     — the PDF/scan is in hand (_stock/NewDocuments/, gitignored)
%    worked-from — held AND built/oracled against (citable as `source:`, §7)
%    in-hand  — held, read, not yet built against (flips to worked-from at build)
%    not-in-hand — named by a held source only; NOT citable until obtained (§7)
%  and `annote` ties the source to the arc/tranche it served.
%
%  Last synced to references.md: 2026-11-19 (v0.61.0, commodity arc opening).
% ============================================================================

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
%  HELD SOURCES — worked-from / in-hand
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

